99
00:07:12,920 --> 00:07:16,500
So at the time they were just looking for paramedics.

100
00:07:16,500 --> 00:07:20,540
And even though technically I'm a nurse, I don't like to really say that I'm a medic.

101
00:07:20,540 --> 00:07:25,420
I'll use that medic license when I have to and this was one of those times, right?

102
00:07:25,420 --> 00:07:26,420
I hate being a poser.

103
00:07:26,420 --> 00:07:29,380
That's what I tell people in interviews like, hey look, I'm not a medic.

104
00:07:29,380 --> 00:07:31,940
Okay, I'm a nurse, but I have a medic license.

105
00:07:31,940 --> 00:07:33,500
And that is 2022.

106
00:07:33,500 --> 00:07:36,740
You can identify however you want to.

107
00:07:36,740 --> 00:07:38,820
Well it all depends on who you say it around.

108
00:07:38,820 --> 00:07:41,500
You say it around that crusty old medic that you're a paramedic.

109
00:07:41,500 --> 00:07:43,060
They all flip out.

110
00:07:43,060 --> 00:07:48,380
But anyway, so I was a paramedic at the time so I was like, okay, I'll go to Ukraine as

111
00:07:48,380 --> 00:07:49,380
a paramedic.

112
00:07:49,380 --> 00:07:56,820
Which was sort of weird because the critical care transport world, most everyone's doing

113
00:07:56,820 --> 00:07:59,980
the same job no matter what your license is.

114
00:07:59,980 --> 00:08:02,140
But they were looking for medics at the time.

115
00:08:02,140 --> 00:08:06,940
So I was able to go there and I flew back from my job.

116
00:08:06,940 --> 00:08:13,300
I was working in the Gulf of Mexico at the time and I had I think 48 hours to switch

117
00:08:13,300 --> 00:08:19,300
out my gear, get my body armor all settled, pulled stuff out of storage and ran around

118
00:08:19,300 --> 00:08:20,580
like a chick with my head cut off.

